  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Each hexagon uses six "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "granny-cluster-hex"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "granny clusters"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " per round, one at each side. After round 3 the hexagon is 9 cm across. Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jayg-cushion"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "join-as-you-go"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to attach each motif to its neighbours on the final round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make 38 full hexagons (19 per panel) in a mix of 4 to 6 colours. Partial hexagons at the edge fill any gaps before the final border round."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "heading": "Materials",
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "DK yarn in 4 to 6 colours",
              "qty": "500 m total"
            },
            {
              "name": "4 mm crochet hook",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Tapestry needle",
              "qty": "1"
            },
            {
              "name": "Scissors",
              "qty": "1 pair"
            },
            {
              "name": "40 cm round or hexagon cushion pad",
              "qty": "1"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hexagon (make 38)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Round 1: ch 4, sl st to join, 2 dc in ring. * ch 2, 3 dc in ring; rep 4 more times. Ch 2, sl st. (6 clusters.) Round 2: sl st to ch-2 sp, "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "granny-cluster-hex"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "3 dc"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", ch 2, 3 dc in same sp (corner), * ch 1, corner in next sp; rep. Round 3: extend as before, joining to adjacent motifs if using JAYG."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assembly"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Lay out 19 hexagons in a flower arrangement for each panel. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jayg-cushion"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Join-as-you-go"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " into a panel. Repeat for the second panel. Place wrong sides together and dc or whipstitch around the edge, inserting the pad before closing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
